MENTOR: We're on Title. This is the frame at 1 s, halfway through its first move.

From 0.5 s to 1.5 s Title moves at one speed the whole way, then carries straight into its next move and stops dead at 3 s: that's linear, and it's why it looks mechanical. Easing slows it out of each key and into the next. With Title's keys showing (U), select both keys of a pair and choose **Animation > Keyframe Assistant > Easy Ease** (F9); the diamonds turn into hourglasses.

Ease Title's two Position moves (0.5 s to 1.5 s and 1.5 s to 3 s), its Scale and its Opacity (both 0.5 s to 1.5 s), and say done. If you'd like to see one done first, just ask.

